# 📊 Simulation Flow

### 1️⃣ Welcome Screen

Introduction to:

- What is a Supply Chain?
- Why Supply Chains Matter
- How Business Decisions Impact Operations

---

### 2️⃣ Random Company Generation

Every simulation creates a unique business with:

- Industry
- Products
- Countries Served
- Demand Level

---

### 3️⃣ Build Your Supply Chain

Make strategic decisions about:

### Suppliers

Choose:

- Single Supplier
- Multiple Suppliers

Learn:

- Cost vs Risk
- Reliability
- Business Continuity

---

### Factory Location

Select the best production strategy.

Understand:

- Manufacturing Cost
- Delivery Time
- Global Operations

---

### Warehouse Strategy

Choose where products will be stored.

Trade-offs include:

- Inventory Availability
- Customer Delivery Speed
- Storage Costs

---

### Transportation Method

Options:

- Road
- Rail
- Sea
- Air

Compare:

- Cost
- Speed
- Sustainability
- Reliability

---

### Inventory Strategy

Choose:

- Low Inventory
- Balanced Inventory
- High Inventory

Learn about:

- Stockouts
- Carrying Costs
- Customer Service Levels

---

# 📈 Live Business Metrics

Business KPIs update instantly after every decision:

- 💰 Cost
- 🚚 Delivery Speed
- ⚠ Risk
- 😊 Customer Satisfaction
- 🌱 Sustainability

Animated progress bars provide real-time feedback.

---

# 📊 Final Executive Dashboard

At the end of the simulation, users receive:

- Overall Supply Chain Score (0–100)
- Strengths
- Weaknesses
- Biggest Business Risk
- Three Practical Improvement Recommendations

